From 22565ecff044179491662ee9812d78f9b47ccc3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:24:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] Cocoa: keep Ctrl and menu links in tables instead of
 associated objects

The instance variables of upstream CocoView, CocoWindow and CocoMenu
were replaced by objc_setAssociatedObject() with OBJC_ASSOCIATION_ASSIGN.
That has two problems:

- the raw Ctrl pointers do not become NULL when Ctrl is destroyed, like
  upstream Ptr<Ctrl> did, and the link of the window was never cleared
  in Ctrl::WndDestroy, while the swizzled canBecomeKeyWindow reads it;
- associated objects need the 10.6 runtime.

Keep the links in plain lists instead: CocoView/CocoWindow -> Ptr<Ctrl>
(with the 'active' flag) in CocoWin.mm, NSMenu -> CocoMenuBar in
MacMenu.mm. The accessor names are unchanged, so callers are not
affected. The owner of a menu item is now found through the items of
live CocoMenuBars, so an item that outlived its bar is ignored.

Remove cocoMenuAction: from AppDelegate and CocoView and
validateMenuItem: from AppDelegate, nothing uses that selector.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
